From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_MM_WIDE, _SWIGLU_REDUCE, _MM_CLUSTER, _MM_DECTILE

ai-engine cbf94fde5 grafted onto the pin stack. MM_WIDE=1|2 takes 128x128 prompt
blocks keeping each output's chain, SWIGLU_REDUCE sums a tiled linear's slices and
applies SwiGLU in one kernel, MM_CLUSTER and MM_DECTILE set the bf16 matmul's
cluster and decode tile; cuda_mm.zig, cuda_mlp.zig, cuda_moe.zig, cuda_glue.zig,
cuda_b16.zig and the glm_mm / glue kernels carry them. Default off: every launch as
the pin has it.

Pin adaptations: the mm kernel keeps the pin's common/qmm_frag.cuh include and adds
glm_swiglu.cuh (the source's glm_qmm_frag.cuh does not exist here); cuda_mlp.zig
already has a local `mm` function, so the module import is named mm_mod; comment
lines single-lined. The source's host policy file and test files are left out (they
target the later build layout); the knob reads stay in the family modules.

Gates on pin+0001..0020: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins green for the touched .cu/.cuh.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: every TF_* setting this patch reads is a row of platform/environment.zig with a line in docs/environment.md, read through cuda.ovn or environment, never getenv. Rows: TF_GLM_OVN_MM_WIDE, _MM_CLUSTER, _MM_DECTILE, _ROUTER16 (u64), _SWIGLU_REDUCE (flag).
- 88267c063 moved GLM's SwiGLU rows into glm_swiglu.cuh with swiglu1<AFTER>: v1.2.7's header stays as it is (the fold's own 15-line glm_swiglu.cuh is not carried), glm_glue_moe.cuh keeps v1.2.7's two instantiations, and SWIGLU_REDUCE's kernel in glm_mm.cu calls swiglu1<false> (GLM's clamp before silu).
- cuda_mm.zig: the Ovn load follows v1.2.7's registry read of TF_GLM_PDL (the fold carried the pin's getenv).
- c0f8e1c4c dropped Kernels.router_part and its unaligned branch (router() refuses unaligned rows first): ROUTER16's branch now sits before v1.2.7's single tile launch with .shared = router_tile_smem.
- source: work/fold/0024-mm-knobs.patch

